   "sentenceId": 10,
   "he": "מַעֲשֶׂה בְּאַבָּא שָׁאוּל בֶּן בָּטְנִית. תָּנָא: אַף בַּמּוֹעֵד עוֹשֶׂה כֵּן מִפְּנֵי בִּטּוּל בֵּית הַמִּדְרָשׁ.",
   "en": "§ The mishna recounted «an incident involving Abba Shaul ben Botnit,» a Sage who was also a grocer, who would fill his measures on the eve of a Festival and give them to his customers on the Festival. A tanna «taught» in a baraita: «He would do this even on» the intermediate days of «a Festival, in order to» prevent «dereliction» of Torah study in «the study hall.» Since he wanted to spend most of his day in the study hall and not have to interrupt his study to carry out measurements, he would measure for his customers at night, when it was not a time of study."
  }
